WEBVTT

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.470
The date is 1969.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.330
The setting is Japan in a period
of advanced economic growth.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.010
This is the story of those who protect
mankind from the grasp of invaders.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.800
This is the story of
the Gate Keepers.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:36.430
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.620
<i>Chikara to chikara butsukareba,
When power collides with power,</i>

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.210
<i>arasoi wa hajimaru.
wars start.</i>

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.760
<i>Tatakau koto ga</i> yuuki <i>to</i>
I <i>don't think fighting</i>

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.760
<i>omowanai kedo...
equals bravery, but...</i>

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.160
<i>...mamoritai yo
...I want to protect</i>

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.720
kimi <i>no sono egao.
that smile on your face.</i>

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:05.340
<i>Asu e no geeto
We can't see the gate</i>

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.040
<i>mienai keredo...
to tomorrow, but...</i>

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.810
<i>dare ni</i> demo <i>aru yo.
one's inside each of us.</i>

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.470
<i>Let's open the gate!</i>

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.190
Kinou <i>no namida</i> wa
<i>The tears we shed yesterday</i>

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.450
<i>kitto muda ja nai.
are probably not in vain.</i>

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.830
<i>Arasoi no nai</i> mirai wa
<i>A future without war</i>

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.590
<i>ano tobira no mukougawa.
waits behind that door.</i>

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.730
Mune <i>no oku</i> fukaku
<i>Retrieve the key lying</i>

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.670
<i>Jitto shimaikonda
deep inside your heart,</i>

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:39.470
<i>kagi wo takaku kakagete,
hold it up high,</i>

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.710
<i>fumidasou!
and step out!</i>

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:46.010
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:52.540
<i>You can open the gate!</i>

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.600
Whoa! It's so fast!

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.160
Hey! You've been
raising your voice...

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.730
...ever since we left Tokyo.
It's embarrassing!

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:23.760
But I've never been on
the bullet train before!

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.040
The scenery keeps zooming by!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.210
Yeesh. Cmon, Reiko.
You say something to him, too.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.910
Huh?

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:39.950
I'm sorry, this is my first
time on the bullet train, too.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:46.030
<i>Thank you for riding today.
The next stop is Nagoya.</i>

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.760
<i>We are arriving at Nagoya.</i>

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.360
Ooh! It's been only
two hours since we left Tokyo!

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.870
That's my super express dream train!

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:57.700
Honestly, would you knock it off?
We aren't here for fun.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.970
I know, I know. We're here to
scout out a new gate keeper.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.820
That's right. The invaders are
getting stronger all the time.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.360
Our highest priority is to obtain
more reinforcements like Reiko!

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.520
Oh, please! I'm not that special!

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.980
But what about you guys, Rurippe?

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.230
What about you guys, Ruriko?

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:31.280
Th- Those? E- Enjoying train lunches
while watching the scenery go by...

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.640
...is what train travel is all about!

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:38.740
Besides, train travel makes
me hungry for some reason.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.490
Reiko, where are you going?

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.690
I'm going to buy a lunch.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.200
Wh- What?!

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.520
Let's see... they say Nagoya
is famous for miso cutlets...

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.400
...but the deep fried shrimp
is also tempting.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:03.200
Wow, they also have
kishimen noodles!

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.200
Hm, let's see...

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:10.210
I've decided. I'll take this
sweet rice jelly lunch.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.420
So that's Himeji Castle!

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.720
Constructed in 1581 by
Hideyoshi Hashiba, Himeji Castle...

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.890
...was gradually restored, thus
bringing it to its current shape.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:32.230
It is also called "Snow Heron Castle"
due to the beauty of its white walls...

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.200
...and is used in movie
and television productions.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.740
Hey, you're right! I saw this
before in a historical play on TV!

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:47.510
Why... are we sightseeing?
What happened to scouting?

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.510
We will do that, of course.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.460
Gate Keeper candidate list 8-374.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:05:01.660
Chotaro Banba, A.K.A. " Bancho."
Okay, let's go scout him right away.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.730
First we have to confirm
his present location.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:12.170
This is a wonderful view.
Can you see the Inland Sea from here?

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.910
Yes, when the weather is good.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.910
Oh, wow. I'd like to see that.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.180
I'm tired of looking at it, myself.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.180
All right then, would you
like to look at this?

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.190
Gate Keeper candidate 8-374
is presently in Nagoyama!

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.520
Hey, is this guy an agent?

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.900
Yes. AEGIS intelligence operatives
are scattered all over the world.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.220
That makes sense.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.180
The deal was to fight one-on-one.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:59.690
Sh- Shut up! It doesn't matter
how l do it, as long as I win!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.630
Wh- What?!
- Why are you Crying?!

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.930
I'm shedding these tears for you.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.470
Wh- What?

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:16.870
I don't forgive those
who break their word.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:20.430
Those who break their word are
worthless human beings. In other words...

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:24.450
...you are worthless human beings!

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.540
Sh- Shut up! Get him!

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.450
Yeah!

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.460
Inner Circle throw!!

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.270
I fought another worthless fight.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.610
Hold it right there!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.050
I'd die if Mom saw me like this!

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:04.080
Get over it! We don't know if
he's a gate keeper or not yet.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.890
The commander had these
specially ordered from...

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:10.050
...the AEGIS costume department
to keep our identities secret.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:11.560
He has bad taste.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.960
Who the heck are you?!

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:18.990
You're Chotaro Banba, right? My
turf is in Tokyo. The name's Ukiya.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.540
I'm O-Ruri the Chain,
and don't you forget it.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:27.010
Hey, you. We came all
this way just to fight you.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:30.170
Wh- What did you say?!
They know me in Tokyo?!

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.770
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:37.010
I can't believe I'm known
in Tokyo! I'm deeply moved!!

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:38.680
What's wrong with this guy?

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:42.420
At any rate,
fight me, Bancho!

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.430
Sorry, no can do.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.260
What? Why not?!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.430
I don't do worthless fights.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.430
Maybe you're just afraid of me.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:58.430
Say what? After hearing that, I have
no choice but to accept your challenge.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.440
That's more like it!

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:06.480
Those are the eyes
of a fighting man.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:11.210
He 's got sharp eyes.
I knew it. He is a gate keeper!

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.380
You're kidding.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:20.490
Come on, hit me
with your best shot!

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.500
All right, here I come!

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.270
Is it a motorcycle gang?

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:37.980
Invaders!

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:45.610
What the hell are those?!

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:46.890
Lets Go!

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.630
GATE OPEN!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.360
Take this! It's an attack l came up
with yesterday when I was sleeping!

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.030
Vacuous missile!!

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:04.240
Oops.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:31.100
Beautiful! She has to be the
reincarnation of Princess Sen!

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.600
Arrow of light!

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.640
Who on earth are you two?

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:43.680
We're gate keepers.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:45.910
Ukiya!

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:50.390
It's okay.just look at
his eyes. He's one of us.

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.990
I'm... one of you?

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:57.900
Huh?

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:03.700
I could die for you!

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.890
O-Oh.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.300
Bancho!

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.170
Upperclassman Hachiman!

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:14.770
You know him?

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:20.010
He is my benefactor!
He opened the eyes of my soul!

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.050
I am defeated'

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.490
Hungry?

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:39.630
Bancho, you have power.
You must use that power...

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.110
...not for yourself,
but for others, understand?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.340
After that day,
I mended my evil ways...

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:50.010
...and became a Bancho
of righteousness!

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:52.840
What's a Bancho of righteousness?

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:56.180
Bancho! I'm glad I ran into you.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.050
Into me?

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:02.680
I'm involved in a movement against Castle
Industries' fill of the salt refinery field.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.560
I came to get you to
help me with the rally.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.970
Don't fill the salt field! The salt field?!
They're going to destroy the salt field?!

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:10.800
Don't fill the salt field!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:15.840
That's right.
Salt is vital to human life.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:19.430
We cannot afford to
lose the salt field!

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:21.610
CASTLE INDUSTRIES

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.650
What is the status of
the opposition movement?

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:30.150
Ignore them, Chief.
What happens to others is not your concern.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:32.080
Yes, but still...

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:35.290
Never mind them!
Ignore all ofthat rubbish!

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:37.760
Just do as I say!

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:41.130
In the three years I
have worked for you...

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.430
...have I ever given
you bad advice?

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:47.300
No. You've got a point. Hmm...

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:52.880
There is a strong possibility invaders
have infiltrated Castle Industries.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.410
We should probably
inform the commander.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.170
If only Reiko were here
in times like this.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:02.820
The invaders are weak
against her piano.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.920
This doesn't seem to be the right castle.
MATSU MOTO CASTLE

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:20.590
Castle Industries experienced a
sudden boom in productivity 3 years ago.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:24.400
Yes. Agent lkusawa, I know this
is an unexpected development...

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.400
...but I order you to
investigate Castle Industries.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.510
Roger, AEGIS!

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:35.540
I want to go with you! My holy duty
is to protect Princess Ruriko!

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.180
Princess Ruriko?

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:41.190
However, I must also assist
with the opposition rally!

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:44.250
I cannot ignore the
request of my benefactor!

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:47.920
What should I do?!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.360
Go with them, Bancho.
The rally starts in the evening.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.930
Really, Upperclassman Hachiman?!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.510
Good for you, Bancho!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:00.740
Hey, we still don't know for
sure whether he's a gate k...

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.680
No, he's a gate keeper.
I'm positive.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.150
How can you be so sure?

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:12.090
A woman wouldn't understand.
Only two men with burning blood...

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:14.920
...who have gone fist to fist
could truly understand.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.860
You didn't actually
go fist to fist.

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.830
Thank you, friend!!

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:25.630
Don't mention it!
We're allies after all!

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.440
If only Reiko were here...

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:34.340
I don't think this is the right
place either. NIJO CASTLE

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:40.170
Sorry about asking for a tour so suddenly.
CASTLE INDUSTRIES

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.980
We have to make a wall newspaper...

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:46.680
...about local well-established
enterprises for Social Studies.

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.480
So, where are the invaders?

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:52.590
Pardon?

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.390
It's nothing, sir!

00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:58.100
I see.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:07.110
What's this place, sir?

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.410
So you are the ones
interfering with our plans.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.640
What?!

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.690
This is what happens
when you poke your noses...

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.120
...into matters that are
none of your business.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.860
He disappeared!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.830
What are you guys?!

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.240
Invaders have appeared
at the salt field!

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.550
Where is the device?

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:46.050
It has already departed the Fuchu base.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.950
It's no good! It won't budge!

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.760
Leave it to me!

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:58.450
Bancho!

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:03.360
Upperclassman Hachiman
is my benefactor!

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:10.670
I must do it also for
Princess Ruriko! I am...

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.810
I AM A GATE SUPER!!

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:18.640
Amazing, Bancho!!

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:20.410
Although it isn't gate ability.

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.810
Check mate, king two.
Check mate, king two.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:29.420
It's an emergency call
from Agent lkusawa!

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.270
They're here!

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.000
But how...!

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:49.640
Yotahachi is always
on an AEGIS transport...

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:52.650
...so it can be available
within 3 minutes of a call.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.810
All right, let's go!

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:57.390
Me, too!

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.920
It's too cramped!

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:14.840
The route over the Sanyo
Main Line is always crowded!

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:20.370
That's it!
Hold on tight, everyone!

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:29.040
NO!!!

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.120
Hey! Drive straight,
will you?! The car will fall!!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.230
Princess Ruriko! Over here!

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:42.090
Eek! Pervert!

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:46.230
N- No, you're wrongl!
I'm only balancing the car!

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.730
Good thinking, Bancho!!
Okay, I'll join you!

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:52.740
N0!!!!!

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:56.440
I'm soiled!
Now no one will marry me!!

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:10.590
What's that?!

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:18.540
Upperclassman Hachiman,
I've come to help youl!

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:27.170
Why did you even bother coming?!

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:30.680
GATE OPEN!

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:33.580
Ultra Cyclone Chopl!

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:38.490
Did it!

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:40.320
Don't let your guard down!

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.610
Why does it have
to be a centipede?!

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:12.360
Rurippe!

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.400
What?

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:21.890
How dare you threaten
Princess Ruriko!

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:23.870
GATE...

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:25.560
...OPEN!

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:28.400
That's amazing, Bancho!!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.200
Although it isn't gate ability.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.810
Did they run away?!

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.330
If only it were that easy.

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:04.780
Oh, my god!

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:10.680
They're trying to engulf
us in a giant wave!

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:13.640
Vacuous missile!

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.090
It's no good!
I'm no match for it!

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.920
That's disappointing!

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:28.090
But I would like nothing better
than to die with Princess Ruriko!

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:30.770
Don't say that! It's a bad luck!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.170
Damn!
lf only l was stronger...

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.400
Ukiya!

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:43.050
Sorry to keep you waiting!
I brought you the gate engine!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.970
The gate engine?!
You mean it's completed?!

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:47.880
What's that?

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.680
It's our greatest weapon,
the one you protected!

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:55.020
The gate engine is a system
which converts and amplifies...

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.930
...gate power into physical energy.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:01.900
The central section includes
the same main engine block...

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:04.940
...which responded earlier to Ukiya's gate.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.440
GATE OPEN!

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:17.440
Ukiya, hurry!

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:19.510
Not yet!

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.610
Ukiya!

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:25.180
Not yetl!

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:28.490
Friend!!!

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:30.030
Just a little longer!

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:34.630
Ukiya!!!

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.600
NOW!

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:40.130
GO!

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:03.920
All right! You did it, Ukiya!!

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.420
Holy crap!

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:15.470
Good work.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.410
In the end, it appears
he wasn't a gate keeper.

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:21.780
Wait a minute. We got
interrupted today, that's all.

00:21:21.850 --> 00:21:24.180
Bancho is definitely
a gate keeper!

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.410
No, he isn't!

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:28.710
Now, now,
calm down, both of you.

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.680
So this is the gate flapper base!

00:21:33.860 --> 00:21:35.190
Bancho!

00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:38.430
What are you doing here?

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:42.930
You know what I'm doing here!
I'm sticking by Princess Ruriko!

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:44.730
Ugh.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:47.930
It appears that he was clinging to
the wheel of the transport chopper.

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:53.510
Are you the commander? Pleased
to meet you! I'm at your service!

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.940
Aah! Commander!

00:21:56.550 --> 00:21:58.950
Commander, make him a gate keeper!

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:03.950
Understood. Your ability is unknown,
so you will be an apprentice.

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:06.590
Thank you!

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.280
Good for you, Bancho!

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:12.190
I'm happy just being
by my Princess Ruriko!

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:14.200
Oh, please, no...

00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:16.460
By the way, where
is Agent Asagiri?

00:22:16.630 --> 00:22:18.470
AH!!!

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:20.630
WE FORGOT!!!

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:25.570
GORYOKAKU
I forget, is Goryokaku a castle...?

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:38.620
<i>Itsumademo wasurenai
We received many things</i>

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:42.490
<i>takusan no mono moratta ne.
we will never forget.</i>

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:47.460
<i>Sora no iro utsushite hikaru
I don't mean the blue jewels flashing</i>

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:50.830
<i>aoi houseki ya
with colors of the sky...</i>

00:22:50.830 --> 00:22:52.970
koinu-tachi
or a big yard

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:58.140
<i>hanemawaru hiroi</i> niwaja <i>nai,
with puppies romping around,</i>

00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:01.480
motto motto daijina
but something <i>much</i> more

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:06.110
<i>mono wo.
important.</i>

00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:10.980
<i>Kinou Kara kyou e
From yesterday to today,</i>

00:23:11.050 --> 00:23:15.610
<i>kyou kara asu e to
from today to tomorrow,</i>

00:23:16.090 --> 00:23:22.390
boku-tachi wa aruite yuku yo.
we will walk toward the future.
